msgid "N/A - Not applicable to this engine"
msgstr "N/A - Kò bá ẹ́ńjìnnì yìí mu"

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "MariaDB 10.11+ and MySQL 8.4+ are the recommended, supported releases for Cacti 1.3.x (available on Rocky Linux 9 through the vendor module streams). Make sure you run the very latest release though which fixes a long standing low level networking issue that was causing spine many issues with reliability."
msgstr "MariaDB 10.11+ àti MySQL 8.4+ ni àwọn ìtújáde tí a dámọ̀ràn tí wọ́n sì ní àtìlẹ́yìn fún Cacti 1.3.x (tó wà lórí Rocky Linux 9 nípasẹ̀ àwọn ṣíṣàn módù olùtajà). Rí i dájú pé o lo ìtújáde tuntun jù lọ síbẹ̀, èyí tó yanjú ìṣòro nẹ́tíwọ́ọ̀kì ìpele ìsàlẹ̀ tó ti pẹ́ tí ó ń fa ọ̀pọ̀ ìṣòro ìgbẹ́kẹ̀lé fún spine."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "It is STRONGLY recommended that you enable InnoDB in any %s version greater than 5.5.3."
msgstr "A dámọ̀ràn GAN-AN pé kí o mú InnoDB ṣiṣẹ́ nínú ẹ̀yà %s èyíkéyìí tó ju 5.5.3 lọ."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When using Cacti with languages other than English, it is important to use the utf8mb4_unicode_ci collation type as some characters take more than a single byte."
msgstr "Nígbà tí o bá ń lo Cacti pẹ̀lú àwọn èdè mìíràn yàtọ̀ sí Gẹ̀ẹ́sì, ó ṣe pàtàkì láti lo irú ìtòlẹ́sẹẹsẹ utf8mb4_unicode_ci nítorí àwọn lẹ́tà kan máa ń gba ju báìtì kan ṣoṣo lọ."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When using Cacti with languages other than English, it is important to use the utf8mb4 character set as some characters take more than a single byte."
msgstr "Nígbà tí o bá ń lo Cacti pẹ̀lú àwọn èdè mìíràn yàtọ̀ sí Gẹ̀ẹ́sì, ó ṣe pàtàkì láti lo àkójọ lẹ́tà utf8mb4 nítorí àwọn lẹ́tà kan máa ń gba ju báìtì kan ṣoṣo lọ."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "It is recommended that you enable InnoDB in any %s version greater than 5.1."
msgstr "A dámọ̀ràn pé kí o mú InnoDB ṣiṣẹ́ nínú ẹ̀yà %s èyíkéyìí tó ju 5.1 lọ."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "Depending on the number of logins and use of spine data collector, %s will need many connections.  The calculation for spine is: total_connections = total_processes * (total_threads + script_servers + 1), then you must leave headroom for user connections, which will change depending on the number of concurrent login accounts."
msgstr "Ní ìbámu pẹ̀lú iye ìwọlé àti lílo olùkójọ détà spine, %s yóò nílò ọ̀pọ̀ ìsopọ̀. Ìṣirò fún spine ni: total_connections = total_processes * (total_threads + script_servers + 1), lẹ́yìn náà o gbọ́dọ̀ fi ààyè sílẹ̀ fún àwọn ìsopọ̀ olùlò, èyí tí yóò yí padà ní ìbámu pẹ̀lú iye àwọn àkáùntì ìwọlé lẹ́ẹ̀kan náà."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "Keeping the table cache larger means less file open/close operations when using innodb_file_per_table."
msgstr "Mímú kí àpamọ́ tábìlì tóbi sí i túmọ̀ sí iṣẹ́ ṣíṣí/títì fáìlì tó dín kù nígbà tí o bá ń lo innodb_file_per_table."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "With Remote polling capabilities, large amounts of data will be synced from the main server to the remote pollers.  Therefore, keep this value at or above 16M."
msgstr "Pẹ̀lú àwọn agbára ìṣèwádìí òkèèrè, ọ̀pọ̀lọpọ̀ détà ni a ó mú ṣọ̀kan láti sẹ́fà àkọ́kọ́ sí àwọn olùṣèwádìí òkèèrè. Nítorí náà, jẹ́ kí iye yìí wà ní tàbí kó ju 16M lọ."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "If using the Cacti Performance Booster and choosing a memory storage engine, you have to be careful to flush your Performance Booster buffer before the system runs out of memory table space.  This is done two ways, first reducing the size of your output column to just the right size.  This column is in the tables poller_output, and poller_output_boost.  The second thing you can do is allocate more memory to memory tables.  We have arbitrarily chosen a recommended value of 10%% of system memory, but if you are using SSD disk drives, or have a smaller system, you may ignore this recommendation or choose a different storage engine.  You may see the expected consumption of the Performance Booster tables under Console -> System Utilities -> View Boost Status."
msgstr "Bí o bá ń lo Cacti Performance Booster tí o sì yan ẹ́ńjìnì ìpamọ́ ìrántí, o ní láti ṣọ́ra láti ṣàn àpamọ́ Performance Booster rẹ dànù kí ètò náà tó parí ààyè tábìlì ìrántí.  A ń ṣe èyí lọ́nà méjì: àkọ́kọ́, dídín ìwọ̀n òpó àbájáde rẹ kù sí ìwọ̀n tó tọ́ gan-an.  Òpó yìí wà nínú àwọn tábìlì poller_output, àti poller_output_boost.  Ohun kejì tí o lè ṣe ni láti ya ìrántí púpọ̀ sí i sọ́tọ̀ fún àwọn tábìlì ìrántí.  A ti yan ìdíyelé àbá ti 10%% ti ìrántí ètò láìròtẹ́lẹ̀, ṣùgbọ́n bí o bá ń lo àwọn àwo SSD, tàbí tí o ní ètò kékeré kan, o lè kọbi ara sí àbá yìí tàbí kí o yan ẹ́ńjìnì ìpamọ́ mìíràn.  O lè rí ìlò tí a retí fún àwọn tábìlì Performance Booster lábẹ́ Kọ́nsólù -> Àwọn Ohun Èlò Ètò -> Wo Ipò Boost."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When executing subqueries, having a larger temporary table size, keep those temporary tables in memory."
msgstr "Nígbà tí o bá ń ṣe àwọn ìbéèrè abẹ́lé, níní ìwọ̀n tábìlì ìgbà díẹ̀ tó tóbi jù yóò jẹ́ kí àwọn tábìlì ìgbà díẹ̀ wọ̀nyẹn wà nínú ìrántí."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "If this number is negative, reduce the innodb_buffer_pool_size until the join_buffer_size turns positive, but allocate approximately from between 25%-50% of memory to the innodb_buffer_pool_size if the database is hosted on the Cacti server, or upto 80% of the systems memory if the database is separate from the Cacti web server.  However, try to not go below the default of 262,144.  When performing joins, if they are below this size, they will be kept in memory and never written to a temporary file.  As this is a per connection memory allocation, care must be taken not to increase it too high.  The sum of the join_buffer_size + sort_buffer_size + read_buffer_size + read_rnd_buffer_size + thread_stack + binlog_cache_size + Core MySQL/MariaDB memory should be below 80% if the database is hosted on the Cacti web server and less if you intend to have very large RRDfiles or hundreds of thousands to millions long term."
msgstr "Bí nọ́ńbà yìí bá jẹ́ òdì, dín innodb_buffer_pool_size kù títí join_buffer_size yóò fi di nọ́ńbà rere, ṣùgbọ́n ya nǹkan bí láàárín 25%-50% ìrántí sọ́tọ̀ sí innodb_buffer_pool_size bí a bá gba ibùdó dátà sí orí sáfà Cacti, tàbí títí dé 80% ìrántí ètò náà bí ibùdó dátà bá wà lọ́tọ̀ kúrò lọ́dọ̀ sáfà wẹ́ẹ̀bù Cacti.  Síbẹ̀síbẹ̀, gbìyànjú láti má ṣe lọ sí ìsàlẹ̀ àkọ́bẹ̀rẹ̀ ti 262,144.  Nígbà tí o bá ń ṣe àwọn ìdàpọ̀, bí wọ́n bá kéré sí ìwọ̀n yìí, a ó pa wọ́n mọ́ sínú ìrántí, a kò sì ní kọ wọ́n sínú fáìlì ìgbà díẹ̀ rárá.  Nítorí pé èyí jẹ́ ìpín ìrántí fún ìsopọ̀ kọ̀ọ̀kan, a gbọ́dọ̀ ṣọ́ra láti má ṣe mú un pọ̀ jù.  Àpapọ̀ join_buffer_size + sort_buffer_size + read_buffer_size + read_rnd_buffer_size + thread_stack + binlog_cache_size + ìrántí pàtàkì MySQL/MariaDB gbọ́dọ̀ wà ní ìsàlẹ̀ 80% bí a bá gba ibùdó dátà sí orí sáfà wẹ́ẹ̀bù Cacti, kí ó sì kéré sí i bí o bá ní èrò láti ní àwọn RRDfiles tó tóbi púpọ̀ tàbí ọgọ́rọ̀ọ̀rún ẹgbẹ̀rún sí àràádọ́ta ọ̀kẹ́ ní ọjọ́ iwájú."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "If this number is negative, reduce the innodb_buffer_pool_size until the sort_buffer_size turns positive, but allocate approximately from between 25%-50% of memory to the innodb_buffer_pool_size if the database is hosted on the Cacti server, or upto 80% of the system memory if the database is separate from the Cacti web server.  However, try to not go below the default setting of 2,097,152.  A sort buffer performs sorts for some queries using ORDER BY or GROUP BY. Configuring sort_buffer_size decides how much memory will be allocated for sort queries.  The sort_buffer_size may need to be adjusted from the default if the workload requires a significant number of sort queries. The sort_buffer_size is defined on a per-session variable.  Use the same equation as that of the join_buffer_size to determine the per connection possible memory."
msgstr "Bí nọ́ńbà yìí bá jẹ́ òdì, dín innodb_buffer_pool_size kù títí sort_buffer_size yóò fi di nọ́ńbà rere, ṣùgbọ́n ya nǹkan bí láàárín 25%-50% ìrántí sọ́tọ̀ sí innodb_buffer_pool_size bí a bá gba ibùdó dátà sí orí sáfà Cacti, tàbí títí dé 80% ìrántí ètò náà bí ibùdó dátà bá wà lọ́tọ̀ kúrò lọ́dọ̀ sáfà wẹ́ẹ̀bù Cacti.  Síbẹ̀síbẹ̀, gbìyànjú láti má ṣe lọ sí ìsàlẹ̀ ìtòjọ àkọ́bẹ̀rẹ̀ ti 2,097,152.  Àpamọ́ ìtòjọ ń ṣe ìtòjọ fún àwọn ìbéèrè kan tí ó ń lo ORDER BY tàbí GROUP BY. Ṣíṣàtúnṣe sort_buffer_size ń pinnu iye ìrántí tí a ó yà sọ́tọ̀ fún àwọn ìbéèrè ìtòjọ.  Ó lè pọndandan láti ṣàtúnṣe sort_buffer_size kúrò lọ́dọ̀ àkọ́bẹ̀rẹ̀ bí iṣẹ́ náà bá nílò iye púpọ̀ ti àwọn ìbéèrè ìtòjọ. A ṣàlàyé sort_buffer_size lórí oníyípadà fún ìgbà kan ṣoṣo.  Lo àkàwé kan náà gẹ́gẹ́ bí ti join_buffer_size láti pinnu ìrántí tó ṣeé ṣe fún ìsopọ̀ kọ̀ọ̀kan."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "When using InnoDB storage it is important to keep your table spaces separate.  This makes managing the tables simpler for long time users of %s.  If you are running with this currently off, you can migrate to the per file storage by enabling the feature, and then running an alter statement on all InnoDB tables."
msgstr "Nígbà tí o bá ń lo ìpamọ́ InnoDB, ó ṣe pàtàkì láti pa àwọn ààyè tábìlì rẹ mọ́ lọ́tọ̀ọ̀tọ̀.  Èyí ń mú kí ìṣàkóso àwọn tábìlì rọrùn sí i fún àwọn olùlò %s fún ìgbà pípẹ́.  Bí o bá ń ṣiṣẹ́ pẹ̀lú èyí ní ìpìlẹ̀ tí ó wà ní pípa lọ́wọ́lọ́wọ́, o lè ṣí lọ sí ìpamọ́ fún fáìlì kọ̀ọ̀kan nípa ṣíṣí àbùdá náà sílẹ̀, lẹ́yìn náà kí o ṣiṣẹ́ gbólóhùn alter lórí gbogbo àwọn tábìlì InnoDB."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When using innodb_file_per_table, it is important to set the innodb_file_format to Barracuda.  This setting will allow longer indexes important for certain Cacti tables."
msgstr "Nígbà tí o bá ń lo innodb_file_per_table, ó ṣe pàtàkì láti ṣètò innodb_file_format sí Barracuda.  Ètò yìí yóò gba àwọn atọ́ka gígùn jù lọ láyè tí ó ṣe pàtàkì fún àwọn tábìlì Cacti kan."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "If your tables have very large indexes, you must operate with the Barracuda innodb_file_format and the innodb_large_prefix equal to 1.  Failure to do this may result in plugins that can not properly create tables."
msgstr "Bí àwọn tábìlì rẹ bá ní àwọn atọ́ka tó tóbi púpọ̀, o gbọ́dọ̀ ṣiṣẹ́ pẹ̀lú innodb_file_format ti Barracuda àti innodb_large_prefix tó dọ́gba pẹ̀lú 1.  Àìṣe èyí lè yọrí sí àwọn àfikún tí kò lè ṣẹ̀dá àwọn tábìlì dáadáa."

#: lib/utility.php
#, no-php-format
msgid "InnoDB will hold as much tables and indexes in system memory as is possible.  Therefore, you should make the innodb_buffer_pool large enough to hold as much of the tables and index in memory.  Checking the size of the /var/lib/mysql/cacti directory will help in determining this value.  We are recommending 25%% of your systems total memory, but your requirements will vary depending on your systems size.  If you database is very large or remote, you can consider increasing this size.  If remote, it can by as high as 80% of the systems memory.  However, cautions must be taken to reduce the swappiness of the system, or to remove swap to keep the system from swapping."
msgstr "InnoDB yóò di àwọn tábìlì àti àwọn atọ́ka mú nínú ìrántí ètò bí ó ti ṣeé ṣe tó.  Nítorí náà, o gbọ́dọ̀ mú kí innodb_buffer_pool tóbi tó láti di púpọ̀ jù lọ nínú àwọn tábìlì àti atọ́ka mú nínú ìrántí.  Ṣíṣàyẹ̀wò ìwọ̀n àpò /var/lib/mysql/cacti yóò ràn ọ́ lọ́wọ́ láti pinnu ìdíyelé yìí.  A ń dábàá 25%% ti àpapọ̀ ìrántí ètò rẹ, ṣùgbọ́n àwọn ohun tí o nílò yóò yàtọ̀ gẹ́gẹ́ bí ìwọ̀n ètò rẹ.  Bí ibùdó dátà rẹ bá tóbi púpọ̀ tàbí tí ó bá wà lọ́ọ̀kán, o lè ronú nípa mímú ìwọ̀n yìí pọ̀ sí i.  Bí ó bá wà lọ́ọ̀kán, ó lè ga tó 80% ti ìrántí ètò náà.  Síbẹ̀síbẹ̀, a gbọ́dọ̀ ṣọ́ra láti dín swappiness ètò náà kù, tàbí láti yọ swap kúrò láti dènà ètò náà kúrò ní ṣíṣe swap."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "This setting should remain ON unless your Cacti instances are running on either ZFS or FusionI/O which both have internal journaling to accommodate abrupt system crashes.  However, if you have very good power, and your systems rarely go down and you have backups, turning this setting to OFF can net you almost a 50% increase in database performance."
msgstr "Ìtò yìí yẹ kí ó wà ní ON àfi tí àwọn àpẹẹrẹ Cacti rẹ bá ń ṣiṣẹ́ lórí ZFS tàbí FusionI/O tí àwọn méjèèjì ní ìṣàkọsílẹ̀ inú láti ṣàkóso ìjábọ́ ètò lójijì.  Ṣùgbọ́n, tí o bá ní iná mànàmáná tó dára gan-an, tí àwọn ètò rẹ kì í sàbà jábọ́ tí o sì ní àwọn ẹ̀dà ìpamọ́, yíyí ìtò yìí sí OFF lè fún ọ ní ìlọsíwájú tó fẹ́rẹ̀ tó 50% nínú iṣẹ́ ibi ìpamọ́ data."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "This is where metadata is stored. If you had a lot of tables, it would be useful to increase this."
msgstr "Ibi yìí ni a ti ń tọ́jú metadata. Tí o bá ní ọ̀pọ̀lọpọ̀ tábìlì, yóò wúlò láti mú èyí pọ̀ sí i."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "Rogue queries should not for the database to go offline to others.  Kill these queries before they kill your system."
msgstr "Àwọn ìbéèrè burúkú kò gbọdọ̀ fa kí ibi ìpamọ́ data jábọ́ fún àwọn ẹlòmíràn.  Pa àwọn ìbéèrè wọ̀nyí kí wọ́n tó pa ètò rẹ."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "Maximum I/O performance happens when you use the O_DIRECT method to flush pages."
msgstr "Iṣẹ́ I/O tó ga jù lọ máa ń ṣẹlẹ̀ nígbà tí o bá lo ọ̀nà O_DIRECT láti ṣe flush àwọn ojú-ìwé."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "Setting this value to 2 means that you will flush all transactions every second rather than at commit.  This allows %s to perform writing less often."
msgstr "Ṣíṣètò iye yìí sí 2 túmọ̀ sí pé ìwọ yóò máa ṣe flush gbogbo àwọn ìgbésẹ̀ ní ìṣẹ́jú-àáyá kọ̀ọ̀kan dípò ní àkókò commit.  Èyí ń gba %s láyè láti má ṣe kọ data léraléra."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics."
msgstr "Pẹ̀lú ibi ìpamọ́ irú SSD òde òní, níní ọ̀pọ̀lọpọ̀ okùn ìṣiṣẹ́ io ṣe àǹfààní fún àwọn ètò tí ó ní ìwà io gíga."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "As of %s %s, the you can control how often %s flushes transactions to disk.  The default is 1 second, but in high I/O systems setting to a value greater than 1 can allow disk I/O to be more sequential"
msgstr "Bẹ̀rẹ̀ láti %1$s %2$s, o lè darí bí %3$s ṣe máa ń ṣe flush àwọn ìgbésẹ̀ sí orí disk léraléra tó.  Àìyípadà ni ìṣẹ́jú-àáyá 1, ṣùgbọ́n nínú àwọn ètò I/O gíga ṣíṣètò sí iye tó ju 1 lọ lè jẹ́ kí I/O disk tẹ̀lé ara wọn dáadáa"

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple read io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics.  Depending on your MariaDB/MySQL versions, this value can go as high as 64.  But try to keep the number less than your total SMT threads on the database server."
msgstr "Pẹ̀lú ibi ìpamọ́ irú SSD òde òní, níní ọ̀pọ̀lọpọ̀ okùn ìṣiṣẹ́ read io ṣe àǹfààní fún àwọn ètò tí ó ní ìwà io gíga.  Ní ìbámu pẹ̀lú àwọn ẹ̀yà MariaDB/MySQL rẹ, iye yìí lè ga dé 64.  Ṣùgbọ́n gbìyànjú láti jẹ́ kí nọ́ńbà náà kéré sí àpapọ̀ àwọn SMT thread rẹ lórí sáfà ibi ìpamọ́ data."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple write io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics.  Depending on your MariaDB/MySQL versions, this value can go as high as 64.  But try to keep the number less than your total SMT threads on the database server."
msgstr "Pẹ̀lú ibi ìpamọ́ irú SSD òde òní, níní ọ̀pọ̀lọpọ̀ okùn ìṣiṣẹ́ write io ṣe àǹfààní fún àwọn ètò tí ó ní ìwà io gíga.  Ní ìbámu pẹ̀lú àwọn ẹ̀yà MariaDB/MySQL rẹ, iye yìí lè ga dé 64.  Ṣùgbọ́n gbìyànjú láti jẹ́ kí nọ́ńbà náà kéré sí àpapọ̀ àwọn SMT thread rẹ lórí sáfà ibi ìpamọ́ data."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "%s will divide the innodb_buffer_pool into memory regions to improve performance for versions of MariaDB less than 10.5.  The max value is 64, but should not exceed more than the number of CPU cores/threads.  When your innodb_buffer_pool is less than 1GB, you should use the pool size divided by 128MB.  Continue to use this equation up to the max the number of CPU cores or 64."
msgstr "%s yóò pín innodb_buffer_pool sí àwọn agbègbè ìrántí láti mú iṣẹ́ sunwọ̀n sí i fún àwọn ẹ̀yà MariaDB tí ó kéré sí 10.5.  Iye tó ga jù lọ ni 64, ṣùgbọ́n kò gbọdọ̀ ju iye àwọn CPU core/thread lọ.  Nígbà tí innodb_buffer_pool rẹ bá kéré sí 1GB, o yẹ kí o lo ìwọ̀n pool tí a pín sí 128MB.  Tẹ̀síwájú láti lo ìṣirò yìí títí dé iye tó ga jù lọ ti àwọn CPU core tàbí 64."

#: lib/utility.php
#, php-format
msgid "%s will divide the innodb_buffer_pool into memory regions to improve performance for versions of MySQL upto and including MySQL 8.0.  The max value is 64, but should not exceed more than the number of CPU cores/threads.  When your innodb_buffer_pool is less than 1GB, you should use the pool size divided by 128MB.  Continue to use this equation up to the max of the number of CPU cores or 64."
msgstr "%s yóò pín innodb_buffer_pool sí àwọn agbègbè ìrántí láti mú iṣẹ́ sunwọ̀n sí i fún àwọn ẹ̀yà MySQL títí dé àti pẹ̀lú MySQL 8.0.  Iye tó ga jù lọ ni 64, ṣùgbọ́n kò gbọdọ̀ ju iye àwọn CPU core/thread lọ.  Nígbà tí innodb_buffer_pool rẹ bá kéré sí 1GB, o yẹ kí o lo ìwọ̀n pool tí a pín sí 128MB.  Tẹ̀síwájú láti lo ìṣirò yìí títí dé iye tó ga jù lọ ti àwọn CPU core tàbí 64."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "If you have SSD disks, use this suggestion.  If you have physical hard drives, use 200 * the number of active drives in the array.  If using NVMe or PCIe Flash, much larger numbers as high as 100000 can be used."
msgstr "Tí o bá ní àwọn disk SSD, lo àbá yìí.  Tí o bá ní àwọn hard drive gidi, lo 200 * iye àwọn drive tó ń ṣiṣẹ́ nínú àkójọpọ̀ náà.  Tí o bá ń lo NVMe tàbí PCIe Flash, àwọn nọ́ńbà tó tóbi púpọ̀ tó lè ga dé 100000 ni a lè lò."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "If you have SSD disks, use this suggestion.  If you have physical hard drives, use 2000 * the number of active drives in the array.  If using NVMe or PCIe Flash, much larger numbers as high as 200000 can be used."
msgstr "Tí o bá ní àwọn disk SSD, lo àbá yìí.  Tí o bá ní àwọn hard drive gidi, lo 2000 * iye àwọn drive tó ń ṣiṣẹ́ nínú àkójọpọ̀ náà.  Tí o bá ń lo NVMe tàbí PCIe Flash, àwọn nọ́ńbà tó tóbi púpọ̀ tó lè ga dé 200000 ni a lè lò."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "If you have SSD disks, set this to 0. Otherwise, do not set this setting."
msgstr "Tí o bá ní àwọn disk SSD, ṣètò èyí sí 0. Bí bẹ́ẹ̀ kọ́, má ṣe ṣètò ìtò yìí."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple read io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics."
msgstr "Pẹ̀lú ibi ìpamọ́ irú SSD òde òní, níní ọ̀pọ̀lọpọ̀ okùn ìṣiṣẹ́ read io ṣe àǹfààní fún àwọn ètò tí ó ní ìwà io gíga."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple write io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics."
msgstr "Pẹ̀lú ibi ìpamọ́ irú SSD òde òní, níní ọ̀pọ̀lọpọ̀ okùn ìṣiṣẹ́ write io ṣe àǹfààní fún àwọn ètò tí ó ní ìwà io gíga."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When using MariaDB 10.2.4 and above, this setting should be off if atomic writes are enabled.  Therefore, please enable atomic writes instead of the double write buffer as it will increase performance."
msgstr "Nígbà tí o bá ń lo MariaDB 10.2.4 àti jù bẹ́ẹ̀ lọ, ìtò yìí yẹ kí ó wà ní pípa tí atomic writes bá wà ní ṣíṣiṣẹ́.  Nítorí náà, jọ̀wọ́ mú atomic writes ṣiṣẹ́ dípò double write buffer nítorí yóò mú iṣẹ́ pọ̀ sí i."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "When using MariaDB 10.2.4 and above, you can use atomic writes over the doublewrite buffer to increase performance."
msgstr "Nígbà tí o bá ń lo MariaDB 10.2.4 àti jù bẹ́ẹ̀ lọ, o lè lo atomic writes dípò doublewrite buffer láti mú iṣẹ́ pọ̀ sí i."

#: lib/utility.php
msgid "MariaDB 11.8 enabled innodb_snapshot_isolation=ON by default. This causes severe lock contention: UPDATE statements can block for tens of thousands of seconds on small tables under concurrent load, which stalls the Cacti poller. Set innodb_snapshot_isolation=OFF in your [mysqld] configuration. See MDEV-39628."
msgstr "MariaDB 11.8 mú innodb_snapshot_isolation=ON ṣiṣẹ́ ní àìyípadà. Èyí ń fa ìjà líle fún ìtìpa: àwọn gbólóhùn UPDATE lè dínà fún ọ̀pọ̀ ẹgbẹ̀rún mẹ́wàá ìṣẹ́jú-àáyá lórí àwọn tábìlì kéékèèké lábẹ́ ẹrù iṣẹ́ alájọṣepọ̀, èyí tí ó máa ń dá olùṣàyẹ̀wò Cacti dúró. Ṣètò innodb_snapshot_isolation=OFF nínú ìtò [mysqld] rẹ. Wo MDEV-39628."

