#: login_providers.php
msgid "Mode"
msgstr "Ìpo Ìṣiṣẹ́"

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Mode which cacti will attempt to authenticate against the LDAP server.<blockquote><i>No Searching</i> - No Distinguished Name (DN) searching occurs, just attempt to bind with the provided Distinguished Name (DN) format.<br><br><i>Anonymous Searching</i> - Attempts to search for username against LDAP directory via anonymous binding to locate the users Distinguished Name (DN).<br><br><i>Specific Searching</i> - Attempts search for username against LDAP directory via Specific Distinguished Name (DN) and Specific Password for binding to locate the users Distinguished Name (DN).<br><br><i>One-Time Passwords (OTP/MFA)</i> - Cacti binds the user password only once, during final authentication.  <i>No Searching</i> performs no directory lookup and binds directly using the Distinguished Name (DN) template, so it is safe for OTP when the DN template alone identifies the user.  When a directory lookup is required to resolve the DN, use <i>Specific Searching</i> with a dedicated service account (or <i>Anonymous Searching</i> where the directory permits it) so the lookup never consumes the single-use code.  For resilient OTP deployments use a single DNS load balancer name in the Server(s) field rather than a space delimited multi-server list, which would re-attempt the bind with an already-consumed one-time password."
msgstr "Ọ̀nà tí cacti yóò gbìyànjú láti ṣe ìdánimọ̀ ní ìbámu pẹ̀lú olùpèsè LDAP.<blockquote><i>Kò Sí Wíwá</i> - Kò sí wíwá Orúkọ Àkànṣe (DN) kankan tí yóò wáyé, kàn gbìyànjú láti sopọ̀ pẹ̀lú ìlànà Orúkọ Àkànṣe (DN) tí a pèsè.<br><br><i>Wíwá Aláìlórúkọ</i> - Ń gbìyànjú láti wá orúkọ olùlò nínú ìwé àtòjọ LDAP nípasẹ̀ ìsopọ̀ aláìlórúkọ láti rí Orúkọ Àkànṣe (DN) olùlò náà.<br><br><i>Wíwá Pàtó</i> - Ń gbìyànjú wíwá orúkọ olùlò nínú ìwé àtòjọ LDAP nípasẹ̀ Orúkọ Àkànṣe (DN) Pàtó àti Ọ̀rọ̀ Aṣínà Pàtó fún ìsopọ̀ láti rí Orúkọ Àkànṣe (DN) olùlò náà.<br><br><i>Àwọn Ọ̀rọ̀ Aṣínà Ẹ̀ẹ̀kan-ṣoṣo (OTP/MFA)</i> - Cacti máa ń so ọ̀rọ̀ aṣínà olùlò pọ̀ ní ẹ̀ẹ̀kan ṣoṣo péré, ní àkókò ìdánimọ̀ ìkẹyìn. <i>Kò Sí Wíwá</i> kì í ṣe àyẹ̀wò ìwé àtòjọ kankan ó sì máa ń sopọ̀ tààrà nípa lílo àwòkọ́ṣe Orúkọ Àkànṣe (DN), nítorí náà ó wà ní ààbò fún OTP nígbà tí àwòkọ́ṣe DN nìkan bá ti ṣàfihàn olùlò náà. Nígbà tí àyẹ̀wò ìwé àtòjọ bá pọndandan láti ṣàwárí DN, lo <i>Wíwá Pàtó</i> pẹ̀lú àkáùntì iṣẹ́ àkànṣe kan (tàbí <i>Wíwá Aláìlórúkọ</i> níbi tí ìwé àtòjọ bá ti gbà á láàyè) kí àyẹ̀wò náà má baà lo kóòdù ẹ̀ẹ̀kan-ṣoṣo náà. Fún ìgbékalẹ̀ OTP tó lágbára, lo orúkọ olùpín ẹrù DNS kan ṣoṣo nínú ààyè Olùpèsè (Server(s)) dípò àtòjọ ọ̀pọ̀ olùpèsè tí àlàfo pín, èyí tí yóò tún gbìyànjú ìsopọ̀ pẹ̀lú ọ̀rọ̀ aṣínà ẹ̀ẹ̀kan-ṣoṣo tí a ti lò tẹ́lẹ̀."

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Distinguished Name (DN)"
msgstr "Orúkọ Ìyàsọ́tọ̀ (DN)"

#: login_providers.php
msgid "The \"Distinguished Name\" syntax, applicable for both OpenLDAP and Windows AD configurations, offers flexibility in defining user identity. For OpenLDAP, the format follows this structure: <i>\"uid=&lt;username&gt;,ou=people,dc=domain,dc=local\"</i>. Windows AD provides an alternative syntax: <i>\"&lt;username&gt;@win2kdomain.local\"</i>, commonly known as \"userPrincipalName (UPN)\". In this context, \"&lt;username&gt;\" represents the specific username provided during the login prompt. This is particularly pertinent when operating in \"No Searching\" mode, or \"Require Group Membership\" enabled."
msgstr "Ìlànà ìkọ̀wé \"Orúkọ Ìyàsọ́tọ̀\", tó ṣeé lò fún àwọn ètò OpenLDAP àti Windows AD méjèèjì, ń pèsè ìrọ̀rùn nípa ṣíṣe àpèjúwe ìdánimọ̀ aṣàmúlò. Fún OpenLDAP, ìṣètò náà tẹ̀lé ìlà yìí: <i>\"uid=&lt;username&gt;,ou=people,dc=domain,dc=local\"</i>. Windows AD ń pèsè ìlànà ìkọ̀wé mìíràn: <i>\"&lt;username&gt;@win2kdomain.local\"</i>, tí a mọ̀ ní gbogbogbòò sí \"userPrincipalName (UPN)\". Nínú àyíká yìí, \"&lt;username&gt;\" dúró fún orúkọ aṣàmúlò pàtó tí a pèsè nígbà ìbéèrè ìwọlé. Èyí ṣe pàtàkì gan-an nígbà tí a bá ń ṣiṣẹ́ ní ipò \"Kò Sí Ìṣàwárí\", tàbí nígbà tí \"Béèrè Jíjẹ́ Ọmọ Ẹgbẹ́\" bá wà ní ṣíṣí."

#: login_providers.php
msgid "uid=<username>,ou=people,dc=example,dc=com"
msgstr "uid=<username>,ou=people,dc=example,dc=com"

